      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what to improve.Now I understand the test. It verifies that:\n1. `Minutes.of(0)` returns the `ZERO` singleton\n2. `ZERO.minus(0)` returns the same `ZERO` instance (identity optimization for zero subtraction)\n\nIssues to fix:\n- Accessing a static field through an instance (`minutes0.ZERO`) is confusing — should use `Minutes.ZERO`\n- Non-descriptive variable names (`minutes0`, `minutes1`)\n- Many unused importsThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces the confusing instance-based static field access (`minutes0.ZERO`) with the proper `Minutes.ZERO`, renames variables to be descriptive (`zeroMinutes`, `afterSubtractingZero`), adds brief comments explaining the intent, and removes all unused imports."
